From 596faf17ad09a4aab1157179a75be2207bff624c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:01:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a static favicon.ico to stop it 500ing in production
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

/favicon.ico has no static file and isn't matched by the next-intl
middleware (paths with a dot are excluded), so every browser's
automatic request for it was falling through to the [locale] catch-all
route with "favicon.ico" as the locale param — which then queried
Payload/Postgres with an invalid locale value and threw, logged in
Vercel as a 500 on every single request (confirmed in production logs
and observability: this was the dominant cause of a 25.8% function
error rate).

Generated from the existing app/icon.svg via sharp + ImageMagick at
16/32/48px, Next's standard app/favicon.ico convention, so it's served
directly with no routing logic involved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NmbMBWtqtKDP2qBMGvpf2h
---
 src/app/favicon.ico | Bin 0 -> 15086 bytes
 1 file changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/app/favicon.ico

diff --git a/src/app/favicon.ico b/src/app/favicon.ico
new file mode 100644
